# OpenShell subscription compatibility

Mitzo personal ChatGPT support is a two-part contract: Mitzo PR #487 is the
consumer, and the production OpenShell gateway must include the reviewed Codex
OAuth broker patch. Stock OpenShell 0.0.116 does not provide that broker.

Before changing the OpenShell CLI, gateway, supervisor, runtime image, provider
profiles, or deployment configuration:

1. Read `docs/operations/openshell-subscription-upgrades.md`.
2. Identify the exact deployed CLI, gateway, supervisor, and runtime-image
   builds. Never infer compatibility from the CLI version alone.
3. Port/rebase the OAuth patch onto the intended OpenShell release and run its
   unit/integration suite before touching production. Do not silently replace
   the patched build with stock upstream.
4. Preserve every upstream persisted protobuf field number. Prove that the new
   gateway can decode a disposable copy of the current production refresh
   records before deploying it.
5. Preserve the provider contract: name `mitzo-personal-subscription`, type
   `openai-codex-oauth`, workspace `default`, and no Mitzo `credentialRef`.
6. Never print, copy, commit, or migrate raw OAuth tokens, authorization JSON,
   headers, or credential databases. Reauthorize through the gateway when a new
   trust domain is required.
7. Use a rollback-capable deployment and pass every smoke test in the operator
   checklist before declaring the upgrade complete.

If the target release removed managed inference routing or `inference.local`,
stop: this is an architecture port, not a routine version bump.
